  Changes: the Sealed image only removes files and replaces the entrypoint script. The changes are
           the Dockerfile and sealed-entrypoint.sh in catalog/apps/internal-tools/images/tooljet-ce
           of this repository (Apache-2.0). No ToolJet source file is modified, so the
           corresponding source of ToolJet is the upstream tag above (AGPL section 13).
           Removed: redis-server and redis-tools 8.10.3 from packages.redis.io with the Redis 8
           modules under /usr/lib/redis/modules (RSALv2/SSPLv1/AGPLv3; Redis is replaced by
           Valkey, decision D-020) and Oracle Instant Client 11.2 and 21.10 (Oracle license, not
           allowed by rule 9). The image is flattened, so the removed files are in no layer.

  Enterprise code: ToolJet's enterprise edition lives in the private git submodules server/ee and
  frontend/ee (ToolJet/ee-server, ToolJet/ee-frontend). They are not in the public repository and
  not in the CE image, whose Dockerfile (docker/ce-production.Dockerfile at the tag) copies only
  build output; the CE server modules for enterprise features are stubs. The manifest lists /ee/
  and the ee paths under license_exclusions, and the image build fails if a file or directory
  named ee exists under /app outside node_modules, so CI fails if they ever appear in the image.

